## 🔗 FOREIGN KEY & DATA INTEGRITY PATTERNS

### **12. FOREIGN KEY RELATIONSHIP HANDLING**
❌ **NEVER ignore missing foreign key references**  
❌ **NEVER skip cross-table consistency validation**  
✅ **ALWAYS handle foreign key constraints gracefully**

```javascript
// ✅ REQUIRED: Foreign key handling pattern
const handleMissingForeignKeys = async (mealLog) => {
  // Check if nutrition_plan_id exists
  const { data: planExists } = await supabase
    .from('nutrition_plans')
    .select('id')
    .eq('id', mealLog.nutrition_plan_id)
    .single();
    
  if (!planExists) {
    // Create default plan or link to user's most recent plan
    const { data: recentPlan } = await supabase
      .from('nutrition_plans')
      .select('id')
      .eq('user_id', mealLog.user_id)
      .order('created_at', { ascending: false })
      .limit(1)
      .single();
      
    mealLog.nutrition_plan_id = recentPlan?.id || await createDefaultPlan(mealLog.user_id);
  }
  
  return mealLog;
};

// ✅ REQUIRED: Cross-table consistency validation
const validateCrossTableConsistency = async (userId) => {
  // Verify all meal logs have valid nutrition plans
  const { data: orphanedLogs } = await supabase
    .from('meal_logs')
    .select('id, nutrition_plan_id')
    .eq('user_id', userId)
    .is('nutrition_plan_id', null);
    
  expect(orphanedLogs).toHaveLength(0);
  
  // Verify all nutrition plans have matching dietary preferences
  const { data: plans } = await supabase
    .from('nutrition_plans')
    .select('id, user_id')
    .eq('user_id', userId);
    
  const { data: prefs } = await supabase
    .from('dietary_preferences')
    .select('user_id')
    .eq('user_id', userId);
    
  expect(prefs).toHaveLength(plans.length > 0 ? 1 : 0);
};
```

